## Portal runtime

Before running any `/upgrade-*` command that starts the portal, the agent reads the workspace `README.md` (or whichever file `runtime.docs` points to) and fills in what it can. These fields are overrides / fallbacks.

- `runtime.docs`: TODO: path to the README that documents how to run the portal, e.g. `README.md`
- `portal.start.command`: TODO: e.g. `docker compose up -d`
- `portal.stop.command`: TODO: e.g. `docker compose down`
- `portal.url`: TODO: e.g. `http://localhost:8080`
- `portal.ready.check`: TODO: URL or log pattern; e.g. `http://localhost:8080/c/portal/login`
- `portal.admin.credentials`: TODO: reference (env var or file path); **never inline the password here**
- `portal.deploy.folder`: TODO: absolute or workspace-relative path; e.g. `bundles/osgi/modules`

