## Database

The agent does **no** database work — it never connects to or upgrades the DB. These fields only drive the Phase 1 docker DB-image alignment and let the agent start the DB container.

- `db.type`: TODO: source DB type — `mysql`, `postgresql`, `sqlserver`, or `oracle` (auto-detected from docker-compose)
- `db.target.type`: TODO: target DB type (may differ from source) — drives the Phase 1 docker-compose DB image
- `db.target.version`: TODO: target DB version, e.g. `8.0` — drives the Phase 1 docker-compose DB image
- `db.name`: TODO: e.g. `lportal`
- `db.container.name`: TODO: Docker container name for the database service; auto-detected from docker-compose if blank

## Search

- `search.engine`: TODO: `elasticsearch` or `opensearch` (auto-detected from docker-compose; the engine type does **not** change in the upgrade)
- `search.version`: TODO: **target** search version — a **concrete** version, e.g. `8.17.4` (not `8.x`). `/upgrade-init` recommends the closest compatible LTS for the target Liferay version (via the compatibility matrix); drives the Phase 1 docker search image tag verbatim

