## Visual & Functional audit

Configuration consumed by the `/upgrade-audit-pages` skill (run manually — it belongs to the frontend / Page-by-Page area; the Phase 5 design is still open). It compares pages between the source and target portals once the upgraded portal is up. The skill reuses `upgrade.source.version` and `upgrade.target.version` for report labels — do not duplicate them here.

- `audit.source.base.url`: TODO: e.g. `https://portal-source.example.com` (no trailing slash)
- `audit.target.base.url`: TODO: e.g. `https://portal-target.example.com` (no trailing slash)
- `audit.user`: TODO: email or screen name used for pages with `requires_auth=true`
- `audit.password`: TODO: reference only (env var or file path) — **never inline**
- `audit.viewports`: TODO: comma-separated; default `desktop`. Options: `desktop` (1440x900), `tablet` (768x1024), `mobile` (375x812)
- `audit.pages.file`: TODO: path to the CSV with the page list; default `.claude/audits/pages.csv` (a starter template is at `.claude/audits/pages.example.csv`)

Calibration log (intentional design system changes the team has already validated and does not want re-flagged) lives inside the skill at `.claude/skills/upgrade-audit-pages/references/known-design-system-changes.md`. Edit that file as the team learns which patterns are intentional.

